# pipe-fanout — A pipes to B and to C; B also pipes to C. C alone
# egresses to master. The pipe topology alone forces the order: A has no
# predecessor, B depends only on A, C depends on both A and B — so A, B, C
# is the unique topological order (§7.4); no tie exists to break.
actor a
gate  A grant a
gate  B grant a
gate  C grant a
cord A -> B
cord A -> C
cord B -> C
cord C -> master
